.TH AD_POSTPROCESS 1 "2026-08-30" "ad 2.0" "ad pipeline"
.SH NAME
ad_postprocess \- dynamic postprocess layer orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_postprocess
.RI [ options ]...
< raw_ops > post_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_postprocess
is the layer plugin host. It reads V2 TSV from stdin, runs a chain of layer plugins, and writes V2 TSV to stdout. The chain is supplied entirely on the command line — there is no manifest or config file for the chain.
.PP
A layer is any executable that reads V2 TSV from stdin and writes V2 TSV to stdout. Layers run in argv order (not sorted, not deduplicated). The same layer can be passed twice.
.SH LAYER CHAIN
.TP
.BI \-\-ad\-layer= NAME
Add a layer to the chain. Layers run in the order they appear on the command line. The same layer can be passed twice (it runs twice).
.TP
.BI \-\-ad\-layer\-path= DIR
Add a directory to the layer search path. Repeatable. Default: bin/ and layers/perl/.
.TP
.BI \-\-ad\-layer\-arg= LAYER : ARG
Pass ARG to LAYER only (not all layers). Repeatable. The arg can contain colons — split is on the first colon only.
.TP
.BI \-\-ad\-layer\-passthrough= ARG
Pass ARG to ALL layers.
.TP
.B \-\-ad\-layer\-profile
Print per-layer timing to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-ad\-layer\-dry\-run
Print the chain and exit without executing.
.TP
.B \-\-ad\-layer\-keep\-temps
Keep intermediate files in a temp directory for debugging. Each layer's input and output is preserved as a .tsv file, and stderr as a .txt file. The directory defaults to /tmp/ad_postprocess_$$ (override with $AD_TEMP_DIR).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-layers
List layers available in the search path and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.SH LAYER RESOLUTION
For each
.I NAME
given to \-\-ad\-layer:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
If NAME contains '/', it is treated as a path (relative or absolute). The interpreter is picked by extension.
.IP 2. 3
Otherwise, search each \-\-ad\-layer\-path directory in order. The first directory containing a file named NAME wins.
.IP 3. 3
If no match, error and exit 1.
.RE
.PP
Extensions recognized: .pl (perl), .py (python3), .rb (ruby), .sh (bash), .js (node). Files without a recognized extension must be executable.
.SH I/O MODES
.TP
Pipe mode (default)
Layers are chained via pipes: layer1 < input | layer2 | layer3 > output. Fastest.
.TP
Temp mode (\-\-ad\-layer\-keep\-temps)
Each layer reads/writes a file: layer1 < 00_input.tsv > 01_output.tsv; layer2 < 01_output.tsv > 02_output.tsv; ... Files are kept in $AD_TEMP_DIR for inspection.
.SH ERROR HANDLING
If a layer fails (non-zero exit), ad_postprocess:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
Prints "layer 'NAME' likely failed" to stderr.
.IP 2. 3
Displays the last 20 lines of the failed layer's stderr.
.IP 3. 3
Exits with non-zero status.
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
No environment variables. Use CLI flags. See
.BR ad_vim (1)
for the config file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --ad-layer=ad_layer_pace < raw.txt
Run reorder then pace.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --ad-layer=ad_layer_indent_last --ad-layer=ad_layer_pace < raw.txt
Run reorder, indent_last, then pace.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer=/path/to/my_layer.sh < raw.txt
Run a custom layer from an absolute path.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer-path=/my/layers --ad-layer=my_layer < raw.txt
Add a custom search path.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer-arg=ad_layer_pace:--delete-pacing --ad-layer-arg=ad_layer_pace:word --ad-layer=ad_layer_pace < raw.txt
Pass args to the pace layer only.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer-dry-run --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --ad-layer=ad_layer_pace
Preview the chain without executing.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --ad-layer-keep-temps --ad-layer-profile --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder --ad-layer=ad_layer_pace < raw.txt
Profile timing and keep intermediate files.
.TP
.B ad_postprocess --list-layers
List available layers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_pipeline (1),
.BR ad_vim (1),
.BR ad_compute (1)
.PP
.I docs/src/plugin-layers.md
\(em full plugin contract documentation.
